//@version=6
// ============================================================
// ZoneEngineV2_W08Core_Worker - W08 Core Identity / Merge / Split worker
//
// Physical home of the W08 persistent index storage and index mutation, kept in its own
// compile unit. It never imports the Main library and never sees the Main Engine: callers
// pass the W08Store plus the primitive values each call needs.
//
// B02 (Repair 04-A): Core identity interval index. One entry per live physical Core (no
// state / Phase / Side filter), key = (bottomTick ASC, topTick ASC, coreId ASC) with
// ticks = round(price / mintick). Physical order only: it never decides Identity. Storage
// is the flat coreIntervalOrderData, stride 4 per entry:
//   [+0 coreSlot, +1 expectedCoreId, +2 bottomTick, +3 topTick]
// Entries always move as whole 4-value groups; a size that is not a multiple of 4 fails
// the call. Each call checks only its own target (entry matched by coreSlot +
// expectedCoreId); the entry is seated at its canonical position by an insertion step.
// No full-index validation, no cap, no bit packing, no array.remove(0) / unshift.
// B04-A: a second index coreIntervalTopOrderData holds the same tuples (same stride-4 layout)
// ordered by (topTick ASC, bottomTick ASC, expectedCoreId ASC); intervalCollect reads both.
//
// B01 (Repair 05-B): Core origin Root membership. One origin Root ID set per physical Core
// (never per Side), kept as a node chain in strict rootId ASC order: real Root IDs only
// (Broad FVG included), no duplicate, no cap. Field names mirror the Main B01 storage. The
// Worker does not own the Core registry: callers pass currentCoreId (ID_NONE = not a live
// Core) and currentGenerationId. Per-Core rows grow on demand up to coreSlot (no cap, no
// slot renumbering). A chain whose head node carries another expectedCoreId belongs to a
// Core that previously used the slot and reads as empty; the first add resets the row as
// the Main slot reset did (its orphaned nodes stay unreclaimed: W08_CARRY_B01_01).
// topologyRevision moves only when a set actually changes. rootId must be an issued Root
// ID (rootId < nextRootId), which the caller guarantees.
//
// B03-A: Inverse-origin index. Candidate source for the Inverse exception only (same FVG
// origin before / after Inverse); it never decides Identity. W07 keeps the FVG Root ID
// through Active -> Invalidated -> InverseWait -> InverseActive (state moves on the same
// slot), so the key is that Root ID (fvgOriginRootId): no synthetic ID, no price key, no
// direction key, Broad FVG not excluded (callers pass canonical FVG Roots only). Storage is
// the flat inverseOriginData, stride 3 per entry:
//   [+0 fvgOriginRootId, +1 coreSlot, +2 expectedCoreId]
// ordered by (fvgOriginRootId ASC, expectedCoreId ASC, coreSlot ASC) as physical order
// only. One origin may map to many Cores. Entries move as whole 3-value groups; a size that
// is not a multiple of 3 fails the call. Collected entries are not checked against the
// live Core registry here: the gather side must match coreIds[coreSlot] == expectedCoreId
// before use (W08_B04_GUARD_02). No cap, no bit packing, no array.remove(0) / unshift.
//
// B04-B: Identity candidate union scratch. identityGatherData holds the old physical Core
// candidates of one new Candidate, stride 2 [+0 coreId, +1 coreSlot], strictly coreId ASC,
// one entry per coreId (coreId is the physical Core identity: never reused, unlike slots).
// The discovery source (Root->Core, interval, inverse) is not recorded and cannot change the
// result. Only Cores that already passed the caller's live guards (W08_B04_GUARD_01..03) are
// offered; the scratch never reads the Core registry. The order is a deterministic physical
// enumeration only: not a comparator key, Identity tie-break or survivor rule.
//
// B06-A: Side Candidate interval pairing (same pass, Support x Resistance, interval gap <= M
// only: no Root / category / inverse test here). Four indexes, stride 3 per entry
// [+0 candidateWinnerIndex, +1 bottomTick, +2 topTick]: per Side a bottom order (bottomTick,
// topTick, winnerIndex ASC) and a top order (topTick, bottomTick, winnerIndex ASC), always the
// same entry set per Side. These physical orders are not the Candidate comparator.
//
// B07-A1: canonical Side matching. Input = the exact PATH A eligible pairs of B06-B (stride 2
// [supportWinnerIndex, resistanceWinnerIndex]); no Root / range test is repeated here. Vertex
// rank = position in the Side bottom order (bottomTick, topTick, winnerIndex ASC); edge order =
// (Support rank, Resistance rank) ASC. Output = the maximum-cardinality one-to-one matching
// whose edge list is lexicographically smallest in that edge order, emitted in that order.
//
// B07-A3: current-pass physical Candidates (temporary storage, not Core identity). One per matched Support x Resistance
// pair and one per unmatched winner, every winner exactly once. Per Candidate: its Support / Resistance winner index
// (-1 = none), tick envelope [min bottom, max top], exact float envelope (stride 2 [bottomPrice, topPrice]), the
// rootId ASC unique union of the winner Root slices (Psych is never a Root) and its first Root ID as minRootId.
// Storage order: matched pairs in canonical matching order, then unmatched Support, then unmatched Resistance, each in
// its Side bottom order (bottomTick, topTick, winnerIndex ASC). This order is storage only, never an Identity order.
//
// B07-B: physical Identity plan of the current pass. physicalIdentityEdges holds every exact Identity edge (stride 3
// [physicalCandidateIndex, oldCoreSlot, oldCoreId]) in canonical order: old rank (coreCreatedTime, coreId ASC), then new
// rank (bottomTick, topTick, minRootId, complete Root set lexicographic ASC; only Candidates with an edge are ranked).
// physicalIdentityMatches holds the canonical maximum continuation matching (same layout and order). The full edge set
// is kept for Merge / Split; the matching only decides ID continuation. Degree-0 Candidates have no row here.
//
// B07-C: ownership plan, one row per physical Candidate (lockstep with the physical storage). Kind 0 = continuation (the
// Candidate holds a selected continuation match: old coreSlot / coreId / generationId to inherit, fresh rank -1), kind 1
// = fresh (slot -1, IDs 0, fresh rank 0 .. freshCount - 1 in fresh allocation order: the new canonical order, then the
// Support and the Resistance winner provenance: presence, Stage, bottom / top tick, minRootId, Root set lexicographic,
// FVG mode, Psych presence, Psych tick). No ID, generation, counter or createdTime is written here.
//
// B07-D: materialized mapping (physicalMaterialized*, written by the Main materialization commit): per physical
// Candidate the final Core slot / coreId / generationId; logical count 0 until a commit succeeds. coreIndexRelease
// removes every Worker entry of one Core (origin nodes reclaimed to the free list, both interval tuples, every inverse
// tuple); coreIndexClean tells whether a slot holds no Worker entry at all (slot-reuse precondition).
// The mapping is logically invalidated (count 0) whenever physicalBuild / identityPlanBuild / ownershipPlanBuild starts.
//
// B08: Merge topology relations (new-centric planning only, nothing applied). One relation per physical Candidate with
// >= 2 distinct old Cores in physicalIdentityEdges (the full graph, never the matches alone), in new canonical order:
// mergeRelations stride 5 [physicalCandidateIndex, survivorOldCoreSlot (-1 none), survivorOldCoreId (0 none),
// absorbedOffset (row in mergeAbsorbed), absorbedCount]; mergeAbsorbed stride 2 [oldCoreSlot, oldCoreId] in old canonical
// order (coreCreatedTime, coreId ASC). The survivor is the B07-B selected match of that Candidate (a fresh Candidate has
// none); absorbed = every other old of its full edge set. Absorbed is a relation role only: never a free decision.
//
// B09: Split topology relations (old-centric planning only, nothing applied). One relation per old Core with >= 2
// distinct physical Candidates in physicalIdentityEdges (the full graph), in old canonical order: splitRelations stride 5
// [oldCoreSlot, oldCoreId, continuationPhysicalIndex (-1 none), childOffset (row in splitChildren), childCount];
// splitChildren stride 1 [physicalCandidateIndex] in new canonical order. Children = every Candidate of the old's full
// edge set (childCount = its degree), the B07-B continuation child included; Merge and Split relations coexist.
//
// B13: PendingTopology (recompute model). The persistent store is the Main W02Aux parent -> child -> Root-list pool,
// passed by reference in PendingTopologyStore. Unit = Identity connected component over live old Cores and physical
// Candidates (full Identity edges, plus old Cores whose existing pending Root lists share a Root ID). A component with
// any old Side in PH_ACTIVE_TOUCH is pending: every live old Core of it is a parent (flag true) whose children are its
// Identity-adjacent Candidates in new canonical order, each child holding the Candidate's complete physical Root union
// (rootId ASC) and the parent coreId / generationId as expected IDs. Reentry = latest-state whole-component replace
// (exact same snapshot = no-op). An inactive component that still holds pending is READY_TO_CONSUME (kept). No
// Merge / Split / Touch plan is stored; corePendingGenerationFlags is not touched.
//
// B14: changed topology scope (I13 dependency closure, planning only). Seeds: every Candidate whose W06 dependency set
// (MEMBER Root -> rootCandComponentIds, Broad FVG Root -> every row holding it as INCLUDED_BROAD, LOCAL or BROAD_ONLY)
// meets the W06 semantic changed current component IDs, or whose Root union holds a semantic changed Root ID; every
// live old Core whose origin Root set holds one; every READY_TO_CONSUME pending parent (pending, component without
// ActiveTouch); all components when the W06 scope is full. The closure is the B13 topology component
// (topologyComponentsRaw). Changed components are numbered in canonical order (components with an old Core by their
// first old in old canonical order, then Candidate-only components by new canonical order, a complete tie between
// edge-less Candidates by the B07-C fresh allocation rank). changedOldCores stride 2
// [oldCoreSlot, component] in old canonical order; changedTargets stride 5 [physicalCandidateIndex, component, ownership
// kind (0 continuation / 1 fresh), oldCoreSlot (-1 fresh), flags] in new canonical order; flags: 1 exact range changed,
// 2 tick range changed, 4 origin Root set changed, 8 Pass1 re-evaluation, 16 pair re-evaluation. Absorbed / retired olds
// follow from the Merge relations and the ownership plan. Nothing else (revision, cache, index) is written.
//
// B15-B1: Core / Side registry. CoreRegistryStore (nested in W08Store.coreRegistry) owns the 109 per-Core / per-Side
// registry fields that were the Main ZoneEngine / W02AuxStore / W08TouchStore storage (Core identity and lifecycle, Side
// state, TouchMark ring, per-Core pending fields, Break / TouchStart snapshots, current Root lists, FVG Side summary,
// corePruneRevisions, sideTouchHistoryTruncatedFlags). Storage only: same names, types and empty initial state as before;
// touchMarkCapacityPerCore keeps default 0 and the Main constructor sets it from the cfg once. The pending child / Root
// node pools stay in the Main W02AuxStore.
// ============================================================
// W09 B06-B2B1 (/17): Side current categoryMask / highMask (sideCategoryMasks / sideHighMasks, sideSlot = coreSlot * 2 +
// sideIndex, default 0) in the SideViewState scalars: the Side winner masks kept for the TouchStartSnapshot (retained /
// pending Cores included). Storage only; the producer is connected later.
// W09 B06-B2C-C1 (/18, I27-18): TouchMark Episode storage, 3 per-mark ring rows next to the 8 payload rows:
// touchMarkTouchNos (int, default 0), touchMarkWeakByDepthFlags (bool, false), touchMarkMaxDepthPcts (float, 0.0) - the
// Episode's own number / depth result. Storage only (W08Touch /4 carries them through append / Merge / Split / apply).
library("ZoneEngineV2_W08Core_Worker", overlay = false)

const int ID_NONE = 0

const int SLOT_INVALID = -1

